          "date": "2026-08-10 11:17:49.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20561 tests: fix lock count retrieval in sanity-flr",
        "message": "LU-20561 tests: fix lock count retrieval in sanity-flr\n\nget_osc_lock_count() matched client OSC namespaces using\nldlm.namespaces.-OST%04x-osc-[-0-9a-f]*.lock_count.\n\nWhen a second client is mounted, another -OST%04x-osc- namespace\nis created, so get_param returns one lock_count value per line.\n\nAssigning this multi-line output to count causes\nlock_count=$((lock_count + count)) to fail with an arithmetic\nsyntax error. As a result, in $(get_osc_lock_count ...), the\nsubshell exits before reaching echo, leaving the command\nsubstitution empty. This causes test_22/test_31 to fail with\n\"unary operator expected\" and \"glimpse requests were sent\".\n\nUse total_used_locks() to sum the lock counts from all matching\nnamespaces. Pass ...-osc-[-0-9a-f] so the helper's *...* pattern\nstill matches client hex instance IDs while excluding OSP\nnamespaces such as ...-osc-MDT*.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial \\\n  testlist=sanity-flr env=MOUNT_2=yes,ONLY=22+31\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial clientdistro=ubuntu2604 \\\n  testlist=sanity-flr env=MOUNT_2=yes,ONLY=22+31\n\nSigned-off-by: Chakshu Kansal <ckansal@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: Ic35b4db13eeb0a64f70e9929603c6c9723ae6bf5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
